    "Micro and Medium Enterprises (SMMEs) comprise 90 percent of all firms (OECD, 2017 ). The significance and contribution of the SMMEs cannot be underestimated in many economies (Resa et al, 2018). In Kenya, the SMME enterprises are the backbone of the economy, they comprise 98 per cent of all business enterprises (KNBS, 2016). Business development is considered in many countries a strategy to create employment and increase the level of income, this is particular in most developing countries. Hyder",
